      "S1"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "For any protein, its native structure corresponds to the global minimum of its free energy landscape (O1), and if another protein has a TM-score ≈ 1 to it, then both proteins satisfy O1 independently.",
    "motivation": "This rephrases H2 to explicitly separate the independent O1 facts from the fold similarity condition, making the logical structure clear and removing the misleading implication.",
    "depends_on": [
