      "O1"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "If two proteins have the same fold (TM-score ≈ 1), and both are in their native states, then both structures correspond to global minima on their respective free energy landscapes.",
    "motivation": "This adds the explicit condition that both structures are native states, which then directly invokes O1 for each protein. It closes the gap by not assuming native state from fold alone.",
    "depends_on": [
